(2883404, 402227, 17507, '<td valign="top">there''s a lot of potential i see in this setup, but i think it''s not fully realized:<br/>- there are no bright/light tones. the photo appears dark and flat.<br/>- there''s noticeably more space on the right than the left. this makes it feel horizontally unbalanced.<br/>- the empty space on the top, especially combined with the tight crop at the base of the pots, makes the photo feel bottom-heavy.<br/> <br/>--<br/> <br/>is this comment seriously not helpful? I fail to understand the reasoning by which a comment reading ''Nice color on color'' is helpful but one that offers specific points of constructive criticism is not.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-10-04 01:19:45.</i></td>', 'there''s a lot of potential i see in this setup, but i think it''s not fully realized:- there are no bright/light tones. the photo appears dark and flat.- there''s noticeably more space on the right than the left. this makes it feel horizontally unbalanced.- the empty space on the top, especially combined with the tight crop at the base of the pots, makes the photo feel bottom-heavy. -- is this comment seriously not helpful? I fail to understand the reasoning by which a comment reading ''Nice color on color'' is helpful but one that offers specific points of constructive criticism is not.', '2006-10-01 17:47:32.000000', '2006-10-04 02:19:45.000000', 1),
