(2896140, 401687, 50231, '<td valign="top">Very Cool Joe! Congrats on the Top 5!</td>', 'Very Cool Joe! Congrats on the Top 5!', '2006-10-04 14:59:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896197, 402196, 45790, '<td valign="top">I see several problems that would have contributed to the poor score. <br/> <br/>Foremost is the poor focus. Being a tightly cropped image doesn''t help. A macro lens is really the way to go if you want to take pictures like this.<br/> <br/>Pictures that don''t make full use of the 640 pixel maximum dimension as a rule don''t score well. <br/> <br/>Very subjective, but I don''t really like the composition. Putting the bee in the frame makes it more interesting, but detracts from the theme. But being only part of the bee is annoying. <br/></td>', 'I see several problems that would have contributed to the poor score.  Foremost is the poor focus. Being a tightly cropped image doesn''t help. A macro lens is really the way to go if you want to take pictures like this. Pictures that don''t make full use of the 640 pixel maximum dimension as a rule don''t score well.  Very subjective, but I don''t really like the composition. Putting the bee in the frame makes it more interesting, but detracts from the theme. But being only part of the bee is annoying. ', '2006-10-04 15:13:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896283, 401157, 61552, '<td valign="top">Wow, you mean I didn''t get last place?  There should be an option to remove the photo even after voting starts.  This one was a spur of the moment crap shoot that I would rather not have in my portfolio.  I wonder who voted me a 10!</td>', 'Wow, you mean I didn''t get last place?  There should be an option to remove the photo even after voting starts.  This one was a spur of the moment crap shoot that I would rather not have in my portfolio.  I wonder who voted me a 10!', '2006-10-04 15:41:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896514, 399229, 8891, '<td valign="top">The premise, costume, model and composition are all very fine. The light is quite harsh on her face, her down turned hand and raised arm. The noise, whether artiscally added or not, distracts me from the models beauty, especially on the white background. I think the frame would have better with a thinner area of black. The images shows a lot of promise and working on your lighting would have helped this a lot. This is all just my opinion and I usually don''t have a clue when it comes to protraiture.</td>', 'The premise, costume, model and composition are all very fine. The light is quite harsh on her face, her down turned hand and raised arm. The noise, whether artiscally added or not, distracts me from the models beauty, especially on the white background. I think the frame would have better with a thinner area of black. The images shows a lot of promise and working on your lighting would have helped this a lot. This is all just my opinion and I usually don''t have a clue when it comes to protraiture.', '2006-10-04 16:52:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896537, 399876, 62895, '<td valign="top">Not Again!lol. Adding to favs.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-10-04 16:01:25.</i></td>', 'Not Again!lol. Adding to favs.', '2006-10-04 17:01:01.000000', '2006-10-04 17:01:25.000000', 0),
(2896712, 402037, 43714, '<td valign="top">very beautiful, congrats to you.</td>', 'very beautiful, congrats to you.', '2006-10-04 17:57:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896754, 402037, 35720, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by PurpleFire:</b></div><hr/><i> I love this shot, but I have a question. Did you use a filter on the front of the 300D or was it applied after in Photoshop? I only ask because I <b>think</b> (don''t quote me) photographic filters are not allowed in Basic Editing. Like I said, I''m probably wrong as no one else has mentioned it. <br/> <br/>I love the comp. The little boat plays well with the position of the sun. This contrast in the clouds vs sky is nice. I love skys that give the feel of montion. <br/> <br/>Congrats, and I really hope it stick. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for your comment. I used red filter when I took the shot and added some colours in post processing, which is allowed in basic editing. Thanks again.</td>', 'Originally posted by PurpleFire: I love this shot, but I have a question. Did you use a filter on the front of the 300D or was it applied after in Photoshop? I only ask because I think (don''t quote me) photographic filters are not allowed in Basic Editing. Like I said, I''m probably wrong as no one else has mentioned it.  I love the comp. The little boat plays well with the position of the sun. This contrast in the clouds vs sky is nice. I love skys that give the feel of montion.  Congrats, and I really hope it stick.   Thanks for your comment. I used red filter when I took the shot and added some colours in post processing, which is allowed in basic editing. Thanks again.', '2006-10-04 18:05:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896879, 402130, 7810, '<td valign="top">Very cool shot !!!<br/>Congrats on the high finish</td>', 'Very cool shot !!!Congrats on the high finish', '2006-10-04 18:43:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2896898, 401497, 41337, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SquishyB:</b></div><hr/><i> I think it would help if the purple was more prominent. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I think this was your biggest problem. I didn''t vote in this challenge or entered but had I entered I would have tried to make purple very prominent. Subtle just doesn''t go well when it''s in regards to meeting the challenge theme. Others seem to hit on some other points which I think are valid but DNMC was your biggest issue, IMO even though there is purple in the shot.</td>', 'Originally posted by SquishyB: I think it would help if the purple was more prominent.   I think this was your biggest problem. I didn''t vote in this challenge or entered but had I entered I would have tried to make purple very prominent. Subtle just doesn''t go well when it''s in regards to meeting the challenge theme. Others seem to hit on some other points which I think are valid but DNMC was your biggest issue, IMO even though there is purple in the shot.', '2006-10-04 18:51:34.000000', NULL, 0),
