(2913569, 401762, 34938, '<td valign="top">Isn''t is amazing that at this time: Current Server Time: 10/10/2006 04:32 AM EDT<br/> <br/>the current third place entry (this one) has been viewed more times than the first and second place entries...goes to show how good this image is!</td>', 'Isn''t is amazing that at this time: Current Server Time: 10/10/2006 04:32 AM EDT the current third place entry (this one) has been viewed more times than the first and second place entries...goes to show how good this image is!', '2006-10-10 05:33:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913624, 401762, 61191, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by montag:</b></div><hr/><i> Why does she have no skin texture (except right around her eyelids)? Very heavy makeup? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>She has a VERY smooth skin in "reality". We didn''t use heavy makeup here: just a hint for the skin and a bit mascara and eyeliner. Finally I used NeatImage for PP that smoothed her skin even more out.</td>', 'Originally posted by montag: Why does she have no skin texture (except right around her eyelids)? Very heavy makeup?   She has a VERY smooth skin in "reality". We didn''t use heavy makeup here: just a hint for the skin and a bit mascara and eyeliner. Finally I used NeatImage for PP that smoothed her skin even more out.', '2006-10-10 07:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913653, 402000, 19959, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>You received some useful comments to the entry and a number of people pointed out the two obvious ''flaws''<br/> <br/>soft focus<br/>Horizontal line<br/> <br/>Overall the photo is nice, it meets the challenge and the purple tone looks believeable rather than contrived (as in some entries) the composition is fine and the lack of a focal point (as commented) is not really an issue in this style of photo.<br/> <br/>I''m assume that the line is a power line or similar, it is a shame it is there and could be cloned out outside of a DPC challenge.<br/> <br/>The focus needs work, in this type of shot you can get away with a little softness, but lack of sharpness (rightly or wrongly) is a number one reason for low scores on this site.<br/> <br/>All in all a nice effort, that could have scored much better with some small improvements. Good work.<br/> <br/>Chris</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... You received some useful comments to the entry and a number of people pointed out the two obvious ''flaws'' soft focusHorizontal line Overall the photo is nice, it meets the challenge and the purple tone looks believeable rather than contrived (as in some entries) the composition is fine and the lack of a focal point (as commented) is not really an issue in this style of photo. I''m assume that the line is a power line or similar, it is a shame it is there and could be cloned out outside of a DPC challenge. The focus needs work, in this type of shot you can get away with a little softness, but lack of sharpness (rightly or wrongly) is a number one reason for low scores on this site. All in all a nice effort, that could have scored much better with some small improvements. Good work. Chris', '2006-10-10 08:32:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913657, 402197, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>Congratulations on a very solid score on this image.  Your idea for this challenge was very creative.  There are a couple of small technical issues that prevented this from making it into the top twenty.  First, the composition looks a little unbalanced, as the negative space above the flower is taller than the stem of the flower.  I think the square crop might not have been the best choice for this image.  Second, your lighting is very effective except for the flashlight you used on the flower.  This produced a couple of hot spots that almost look like pollen or something lying on the flower.  If you could have found a way to bounce this light or diffuse it somehow, it really would have given you a bit more flexibility in post processing to bring more pop to  the purple in the flower.  <br/> <br/>I really would like to encourage you to revisit this image now that you aren''t handcuffed by the basic editing rules.  By changing the crop and tweaking the flower, you will have something worthy of hanging on your wall.  Nicely done.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, Congratulations on a very solid score on this image.  Your idea for this challenge was very creative.  There are a couple of small technical issues that prevented this from making it into the top twenty.  First, the composition looks a little unbalanced, as the negative space above the flower is taller than the stem of the flower.  I think the square crop might not have been the best choice for this image.  Second, your lighting is very effective except for the flashlight you used on the flower.  This produced a couple of hot spots that almost look like pollen or something lying on the flower.  If you could have found a way to bounce this light or diffuse it somehow, it really would have given you a bit more flexibility in post processing to bring more pop to  the purple in the flower.   I really would like to encourage you to revisit this image now that you aren''t handcuffed by the basic editing rules.  By changing the crop and tweaking the flower, you will have something worthy of hanging on your wall.  Nicely done. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim ', '2006-10-10 08:36:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913684, 402186, 19959, '<td valign="top">Greetingds from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>OK. Great photo, underrated... why?<br/> <br/>Well... voters can be a fickle bunch, this is a nice shot, the negative space works well and the lighting is good. OK, so it''s just a shot of a guy in a Purple shirt, but it works as a composition and is overall interesting to the viewer.... <br/> <br/>Cropping the top so close to (on) the guys head was a mistake IMO. He needs a little more space above him...<br/> <br/>The sock is not distracting, in fact it helps the composition in my opinion.<br/> <br/>Voters will often mark down a shot if it is not classically well composed, which hit your score.. some monitors are also darker than others which can cause negative scores if the shot appears dark.. (It Looks perfect on my PC and MAC BTW)<br/> <br/>Overall, nice work, I like it and a lot of voters did also.. perhaps it needs a little more of a story.. i.e. have him wear a color sock that clashed.. and leave the viewer to decide why he has done it... <br/> <br/>Chris<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetingds from the Critique Club OK. Great photo, underrated... why? Well... voters can be a fickle bunch, this is a nice shot, the negative space works well and the lighting is good. OK, so it''s just a shot of a guy in a Purple shirt, but it works as a composition and is overall interesting to the viewer....  Cropping the top so close to (on) the guys head was a mistake IMO. He needs a little more space above him... The sock is not distracting, in fact it helps the composition in my opinion. Voters will often mark down a shot if it is not classically well composed, which hit your score.. some monitors are also darker than others which can cause negative scores if the shot appears dark.. (It Looks perfect on my PC and MAC BTW) Overall, nice work, I like it and a lot of voters did also.. perhaps it needs a little more of a story.. i.e. have him wear a color sock that clashed.. and leave the viewer to decide why he has done it...  Chris ', '2006-10-10 08:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913712, 399229, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>Congratulations on a solid score for your first challenge entry.  As you can tell from the comments you received during the challenge, large borders are a love it or hate thing at DPC.  The real disadvantage of such a large border is that it reduces the viewable size of the image for the voter.  The smaller the image, the less time the voters are willing to spend looking at the image.<br/> <br/>As for what could be done to improve your score.  I think you achieved your intent for this image very well.  It has a very artistic feel to it, with the desaturated colors and the film grain look.  However, both of these effects generally don''t score that well at DPC.  It seems that the majority of voters like saturated colors and sharp images.  So what do you do, stay true to your style or change for a better score?  I encourage you stay true to your style, as images like this are appreciated by many members of this site.  Just remember not to take the scores personally, as they will not reflect the true quality of your work.  Thanks for submitting this image.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, Congratulations on a solid score for your first challenge entry.  As you can tell from the comments you received during the challenge, large borders are a love it or hate thing at DPC.  The real disadvantage of such a large border is that it reduces the viewable size of the image for the voter.  The smaller the image, the less time the voters are willing to spend looking at the image. As for what could be done to improve your score.  I think you achieved your intent for this image very well.  It has a very artistic feel to it, with the desaturated colors and the film grain look.  However, both of these effects generally don''t score that well at DPC.  It seems that the majority of voters like saturated colors and sharp images.  So what do you do, stay true to your style or change for a better score?  I encourage you stay true to your style, as images like this are appreciated by many members of this site.  Just remember not to take the scores personally, as they will not reflect the true quality of your work.  Thanks for submitting this image. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-10-10 09:22:19.000000', NULL, 0),
